// Driver-agreement REJECT side (the #433-inverse): a well-typedness judgment is
// ONE static fact, so an ill-typed program must be REJECTED identically by every
// driver — `--dump`, `--interpret`, and `--native`. This program is deliberately
// ill-typed (`integer + text` has no operator); the oracle asserts all three
// drivers reject it (none runs, same diagnostic), exercising the reject facet the
// all-accept corpus never touches.
//
// @ORACLE_STATIC_REJECT: the reject IS the subject — this program must not compile, and
// the oracle's claim is that all three drivers refuse it identically.
fn main() {
    x = 1;
    y = x + "text";
    println("{y}");
}
